From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 09:33:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Describe the trackpad actuator

The J604 MTP coprocessor announces an actuator interface next to
multi-touch, keyboard and stm (J604 ADT 25G83:
/arm-io/dockchannel-mtp/mtp-transport/actuator, device_type "actuator").
dockchannel-hid creates a HID device only for interfaces that have a child
node, so on the J604 the actuator is dropped ("No OF node for subdevice
actuator, ignoring" at debug level) and hid-magicmouse runs without one:
its force-feedback effects and the optional host-driven click
(hid_magicmouse.haptic_press) have nothing to drive. Every other MTP
trackpad board in the tree (t8112 J413/J415/J493, t8122 J504, t602x,
t603x, t604x J614/J616, t6041 J616c) describes it the same way.

Add the empty actuator node. hid-apple-mtp-haptic then binds the
"Apple MTP actuator" device and asserts device-controlled mode at probe
(the mode the part powers up in), so the firmware keeps playing its own
click as today. apple,click-strength is left out until the J604 firmware's
own strength has been read back and a value chosen on the machine.

The ADT also lists tp-accel; it has no consumer driver and is left out.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
index 6d6a90c1ba..79870fa6f6 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
@@ -395,6 +395,17 @@
 
 	stm {
 	};
+
+	/*
+	 * The trackpad haptic actuator (J604 ADT
+	 * /arm-io/dockchannel-mtp/mtp-transport/actuator). Without this node
+	 * dockchannel-hid ignores the interface the coprocessor announces, so
+	 * hid-magicmouse finds no actuator for its force-feedback effects.
+	 * No apple,click-strength: the firmware keeps its own click strength
+	 * until a J604 value is measured.
+	 */
+	actuator {
+	};
 };
 
